---
description: Apply when working on HADES plugins, Plugin Manager, Tool Router, service lifecycle, dependency installation or .HadesPlugin packages
alwaysApply: false
---
- Read `docs/PLUGIN_RUNTIME_CONTRACT.md` before changing plugin behavior.
- The Plugin page and autonomous AI must use the same execution engine and persisted tool-call model.
- Global `block` policy always wins. Manual runs require explicit user approval. Autonomous runs never silently convert `ask` into approval.
- Execute argv arrays with `shell=False`; never concatenate user input into a shell command.
- A service `start` succeeds only after its declared healthcheck passes. Exit code 0 alone is not health proof.
- Persist status, stdout, stderr, exit code, duration, timestamps, invocation type and approval state.
- Dependency failure must remain visible and must not leave a plugin falsely Ready/enabled.
- Do not claim OS sandboxing: current permission enforcement is application-level.
